If work does not map to an approved feature, raise `[Scope Drift]` via AskQuestion:
- Cite the code or file being created
- Explain which feature it was intended for
- First option: "Map to feature FN — here's why..."
- Last option: "Let me explain / provide more context"

### Out of Scope (do not implement)

Document permanent exclusions in `docs/spec.md` §Non-Goals and `docs/feature-list.md`.
Do not implement capabilities listed there without an evolve cycle (16-evolve).

**Migration non-goal (REQ-016)**: No product feature rewrites during monorepo migration.
Structural moves and wiring only — behavior of F1–F4 must remain unchanged until F6 cutover.

## Component Verification

New files must map to an approved component from `[Corpus: system-spec]`
(`docs/spec.md` §Component Overview):

| Component | Location |
|-----------|----------|
| Backend API | `apps/backend/` |
| Frontend | `apps/frontend/` |
| Worker (F8) | `apps/worker/` |
| E2E workspace | `apps/e2e/` |
| Auth library | `packages/auth/` |
| tac2iwxxm | `packages/tac2iwxxm/` |
| tac-validate | `packages/tac-validate/` |
| iwxxm-validate | `packages/iwxxm-validate/` |
| Dissemination (F16–F19) | `packages/dissemination/` |
| Shared | `packages/shared/` |
| Vendor schemas | `vendor/schemas/*` (read-only) |
| gifts (transitional) | `packages/gifts/` until F6 cutover delete |

Files outside approved locations require justification. Raise `[Scope Drift]` if a new
component is introduced that is not in the spec.

During migration, legacy paths (`backend/`, `frontend/`, `GIFTs/`, `auth/`, `schemas/`)
are transitional only — new work targets the monorepo tree above.

## Dependency Verification

Before adding any new dependency, check `[Corpus: tech-spec]` → `docs/dependency-inventory.md`.
If the dependency is not listed:
1. Raise `[Decision]` with a recommendation
2. On approval, back-add to `docs/dependency-inventory.md`
3. Record the decision in `workflow-state.yaml` §`decisions_log`

## Browser Connectivity

Frontend-facing API changes must trace to connectivity tasks in the execution plan and
`docs/test-plan.md` tiers **H4–H5** (plus **H6′** for UJ-027–030 when F16–F19 ships).
See [connectivity-gates.md](../../skills/connectivity-gates.md). Dissemination drawer work
without H4–H5/H6′ tasks is `[Scope Drift]` unless waived by ADR/AskQuestion.

## Dissemination (F16–F19)

- One-shot BYOC destination credentials are **memory-only** — never persist to F5 sessions,
  logs, or saved profiles (ADR-021 amend; ADR-029).
- Egress is **backend-mediated** with required `DISSEMINATION_EGRESS_ALLOWLIST` (empty ⇒ deny).
- Do **not** reintroduce in-app paste of Supabase **auth** keys.
- F8 worker must **not** auto-push ingest results; operator push sinks are F16–F19 only.
- Optional rule: [dissemination-egress-ssrf.mdc](../optional/dissemination-egress-ssrf.mdc).
